  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B051",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B009",
    "B020"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration has changed from B009 to B051. Squeezed light remains a profound and mature quantum-optical achievement, but the discussion makes its experimental attribution boundary less secure than I had initially judged. Optical lattice clocks instead unite a sharply identifiable physical idea, decisive realization, independent reproducibility, and a stable new regime of precision measurement. Katori and Ye provide the most coherent two-person allocation on the present record, provided that the citation remains confined to lattice-clock invention and realization rather than later standards or applications.",
    "case_against": "The decisive remaining reservation is historical attribution: a final priority review must confirm that no indispensable early contributor is omitted. The achievement is a measurement platform, so its case should rest on the demonstrated suppression and control of clock shifts and the resulting precision-physics capability, not on prospective institutional consequences such as redefinition of the second.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that optical lattice clocks have an unusually direct chain from Katori's magic-wavelength concept to Ye's decisive experimental development, with mature reproducibility and compact attribution.",
        "response": "I now agree that this combination is decisive in the final comparison. A basic quantum limit or systematic perturbation becomes controllable in a way that has survived independent laboratory testing; that is a powerful form of maturity. The historical review should still test the two-person allocation, but B051 presently offers the clearest correspondence between the foundational advance, demonstrated physical performance, and exact credit."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce concludes that B051 is preferable to IceCube and squeezed light because its defining concept and realization are less entangled with collaboration-scale or distributed-development attribution.",
        "response": "I share that conclusion without treating breadth of support as a scientific criterion. The issue is not that B009 or B006 lack merit; it is that their proposed named allocations must represent a much wider chain of essential experimental work. B051 is more sharply delimited while retaining exceptional scientific maturity and reach."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth stresses that the physical achievement is reproducible suppression of lattice-induced clock shifts, rather than future standards applications, and compares it favorably with the broader theoretical scope of B020.",
        "response": "This is the right citation discipline. It preserves the discovery-level content of B051 and avoids awarding a community-wide metrological infrastructure. I continue to regard Cirac and Zoller as an exceptionally clean theoretical alternative, but the lattice-clock result more directly joins a distinct concept to repeatedly demonstrated quantitative performance."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether contemporaneous priority evidence confirms that Katori and Ye alone encompass the indispensable conceptual and experimental contributions to the original optical-lattice-clock achievement.",
      "Whether the final citation can precisely distinguish lattice-clock invention and realization from broader optical-clock, frequency-metrology, and standards developments.",
      "Whether a later historical review of squeezed-light experiments would establish a more defensible experimental allocation for B009."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No direct conflict with the proposed laureates is apparent. My professional work in quantum technology heightens my interest in B009 and B020, but neither is my final proposed configuration; I have reassessed B051 on the supplied scientific and attribution record."
  }
}
